OL,3,GNEWSAHigh-risk domestic abusers will
OL,4,Ahave sessions to manage emotions
OL,5,
OL,6,FHigh-risk domestic violence
OL,7,Fperpetrators will have one-to-one
OL,8,Fsessions on how to manage their
OL,9,Femotions, as part of a new scheme.
OL,11,FThe Drive Project will be introduced
OL,12,Facross Cambridgeshire and is aimed at
OL,13,Fabusers who pose the greatest risk to
OL,14,Ftheir victims, children and
OL,15,Fcommunities.
OL,17,FIt is funded by the Home Office as part
OL,18,Fof the government's violence against
OL,19,Fwomen and girls strategy, in a bid to
OL,20,Fstop reoffending. Survivors will also
OL,21,Freceive dedicated emotional and
OL,22,Fpractical support.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
